            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Toast {{cumin-seeds}} of cumin seeds in a dry pan for 1 minute until fragrant and slightly darker. Set aside to cool."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Grate the half cucumber and squeeze the grated flesh in a clean cloth or your hands to remove as much liquid as possible."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir together {{plain-yoghurt}} of yogurt, the squeezed cucumber, {{mint}} of chopped mint, and the toasted cumin in a bowl. Season with salt and a pinch of black pepper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Taste and adjust salt. Chill for at least 30 minutes before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "symptom": "Raita is watery",
              "cause": "Cucumber not squeezed dry before mixing",
              "fix": "Always squeeze grated cucumber firmly in a cloth before adding to the yogurt. Even if it looks dry, cucumber releases more liquid as it sits."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Yogurt is too thin",
              "cause": "Low-fat yogurt used",
              "fix": "Full-fat thick yogurt gives the right consistency. If using a thinner yogurt, strain it through a cloth for 20 minutes first."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Raita is the cooling counterpart to the hot, spiced main dishes of the South Asian table. In British curry houses it is served as a side dish, often alongside poppadoms and chutney. The cucumber version is the most common in British restaurants; Indian domestic cooking uses dozens of variations including banana, boondi (fried chickpea flour balls), and roasted aubergine."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
